      "answer": "$A=(3,2,1)$ and the required plane is $7x+5y-4z=27$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Find $A$: EITHER substitute $y=2$ in both plane equations and solve for $x$ or $z$ - (M1; obtain $x=3$ and $z=1$ - A1). OR find the equation of the line of intersection, substitute $y=2$ in the line equation and solve for $x$ or $z$ - (M1; obtain $x=3$ and $z=1$ - A1). Find the plane: EITHER use scalar products to obtain equations such as $a+b+3c=0$ - (B1; form a second equation such as $2a-2b+c=0$ and solve for one ratio - *M1; obtain $a:b:c=7:5:-4$ - A1; use coordinates of $A$ in the general equation and find $d$ - DM1; obtain $7x+5y-4z=27$, or equivalent - A1 FT). OR1 calculate the vector product $(\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}+3\\mathbf{k})\\times(2\\mathbf{i}-2\\mathbf{j}+\\mathbf{k})$ - (*M1; obtain two correct components - A1; obtain $7\\mathbf{i}+5\\mathbf{j}-4\\mathbf{k}$ - A1; substitute coordinates of $A$ and find $d$ - DM1; obtain $7x+5y-4z=27$, or equivalent - A1 FT). OR2 form a two-parameter equation for the plane - (*M1; state a correct equation such as $\\mathbf{r}=3\\mathbf{i}+2\\mathbf{j}+\\mathbf{k}+\\lambda(\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}+3\\mathbf{k})+\\mu(2\\mathbf{i}-2\\mathbf{j}+\\mathbf{k})$ - A1 FT; state three correct equations in $x,y,z,\\lambda,\\mu$ - A1 FT; eliminate $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$ - DM1; obtain $7x+5y-4z=27$, or equivalent - A1 FT). OR3 use the direction vector of the line of intersection as the plane normal - (*M1; obtain two correct components - A1; obtain three correct components - A1; substitute coordinates of $A$ and find $d$ - DM1; obtain $7x+5y-4z=27$, or equivalent - A1 FT). Total: 7.",
